1
00:00:01,070 --> 00:00:03,270
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:03,550 --> 00:00:04,010
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:09,250
My name is Catherine and today we're traveling a little bit and we need to book a hotel room.

4
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:09,830
That's right.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:17,760
So today we're going to learn all the words and phrases that will help you talk to the receptionist in order to book a hotel room.

6
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,590
Let's check out our dialogue.

7
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,760
Madison Suites, how may I help you?

8
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:29,040
Yes, I am calling from Mexico.

9
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:33,120
I will be in town next week and would like to know if you have availability?

10
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:34,820
Ok, ma'am.

11
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:37,080
Can you tell me the date you expect to check in?

12
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:38,580
Yes, July ninth.

13
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,100
I will be there for seven nights.

14
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:44,610
We have a junior single suite or a superior double suite available for those dates.

15
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:45,770
What's the difference?

16
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:50,710
The junior suite is smaller and has one twin bed, while the superior suite has a double bed and minibar.

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:53,760
Ok, I would like to reserve the superior suite.

18
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:54,630
Is breakfast included?

19
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,520
Yes, a buffet breakfast is served every morning.

20
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:00,430
I will need your name and your credit card details in order to complete the reservation.

21
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:01,350
Sure.

22
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:03,390
My credit card number is...

23
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,480
All right.

24
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:08,020
We're back.

25
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,800
So now let's take a look at language takeaway.

26
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:13,250
Language takeaway.

27
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:18,580
So we've got a lot of great phrases and words today in language takeaway.

28
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,660
The first one comes from the beginning of the dialogue.

29
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:22,960
It's availability.

30
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:24,560
All right.

31
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:27,860
So the woman wanted to know if the hotel has availability.

32
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,300
So what does that mean?

33
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,670
That means, do you have free rooms?

34
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:34,630
Do you have any rooms I could rent?

35
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:39,150
So instead of saying, do you have any free rooms or do you have rooms available?

36
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,730
You can just say, do you have availability?

37
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,800
That's right.

38
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:47,350
So you're basically asking the person, do you have anything available?

39
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,110
So what's your availability?

40
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:50,490
Very good.

41
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:52,320
Okay.

42
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,320
All right.

43
00:01:53,320 --> 00:02:01,320
So we have availability and obviously the receptionist needs to know when we expect to check in.

44
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:05,870
So this is a noun and a verb, but in today's dialogue, it's used as a verb.

45
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,730
So it's something we do to check in.

46
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:13,570
So the person on the phone would like to know what date you expect to check in.

47
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:16,590
That means when will you arrive at our hotel?

48
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:17,150
That's right.

49
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:22,570
So maybe we will arrive to the city a couple of days before we check into the hotel.

50
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:27,640
So we really specifically want to know when are you going to start sleeping here?

51
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:27,810
That's right.

52
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:33,230
And the opposite, so when you leave the hotel, is called check out, to check out.

53
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:33,910
That's right.

54
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:35,680
Okay.

55
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:44,280
So we want to check in on July 9th and the receptionist tells us that we have available a single suite or a double suite.

56
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,280
All right.

57
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,130
So these are two different kinds of rooms.

58
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:55,050
Now a suite is different from a room because it actually means that the space you're going to use is more than one room, maybe two rooms or three.

59
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:55,810
That's right.

60
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:58,310
So it's a little bit bigger than just a standard room.

61
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:03,210
It might have a sitting area or a kitchen area.

62
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:05,170
So that's what a suite is.

63
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,680
Very expensive rooms are suites as well.

64
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:12,230
They have a sitting area and a kitchen and maybe even an extra bedroom.

65
00:03:12,490 --> 00:03:12,970
That's right.

66
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:13,860
Okay.

67
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,600
So we have a single suite.

68
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:20,180
That means that we have one of these big rooms that is only for one person.

69
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:24,780
And the double suite means that two or more people can sleep there.

70
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:25,220
That's right.

71
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:28,680
So single will be one person and double will be two people.

72
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:37,620
And we also heard similar words with the beds because sometimes the rooms aren't really clear about what kind of beds they have.

73
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,940
So this person asked, what's the difference between these rooms?

74
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:46,480
And the hotel employee answered, well, the junior suite has one twin bed.

75
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,080
All right.

76
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:49,570
What's a twin bed?

77
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:54,730
So a twin bed is basically a bed that's only for one person.

78
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,090
Only one person fits in there.

79
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:56,470
All right.

80
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:59,310
So it's a single bed basically.

81
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,600
We call it a twin.

82
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:01,810
It's a standard size.

83
00:04:02,170 --> 00:04:04,950
So everywhere you go, a twin is always for one person.

84
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:05,690
That's right.

85
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:06,370
All right.

86
00:04:06,370 --> 00:04:09,710
And if you want to have another person in bed, we have to get a bigger one.

87
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:10,870
And what's that bigger bed called?

88
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:12,210
It's called a double bed.

89
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:13,310
A double bed.

90
00:04:13,510 --> 00:04:14,230
So again, double.

91
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:16,430
Double room, double bed.

92
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,200
So this means that two people can sleep on the one bed.

93
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:20,960
That's right.

94
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:28,540
So this is important because sometimes you want to book a hotel room and it will be a double suite, but it will have two twin beds.

95
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:29,200
All right.

96
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,360
So it's a double room.

97
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:33,820
So it's for two people, but each person has their own small bed.

98
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,240
That's right.

99
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:35,500
Two twin beds.

100
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,240
Mm-hmm.

101
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,240
Okay.

102
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:44,600
And lastly, the superior double suite not only had a double bed, but also had a mini bar.

103
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,000
A mini bar.

104
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,160
So you know what a bar is?

105
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:51,800
It's a place you go to get some alcohol or some drinks, but a mini bar is a little bit different, right?

106
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,240
Mm-hmm.

107
00:04:53,240 --> 00:05:04,320
It's a little refrigerator or a little area where you will have snacks and drinks that you can just basically take freely, but obviously you will have to pay afterwards.

108
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,120
That's right.

109
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:11,700
So you can take them when you're staying there, but when you check out, when you leave, you have to pay for everything you ate or drank.

110
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:12,450
That's right.

111
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,280
Okay.

112
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:15,800
So a lot of words there on Language Takeaway today.

113
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,810
Let's take a break and listen to the dialogue again.

114
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:23,640
Madison Suites, how may I help you?

115
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,980
Yes, I am calling from Mexico.

116
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:32,240
I will be in town next week and would like to know if you have availability.

117
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:33,240
Okay, ma'am.

118
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,640
Can you tell me the date you expect to check in?

119
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,540
Yes, July 9th.

120
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,080
I will be there for seven nights.

121
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:44,440
We have a junior single suite or a superior double suite available for those dates.

122
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:44,900
What's the difference?

123
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:50,160
The junior suite is smaller and has one twin bed while the superior suite has a double bed and mini bar.

124
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:50,360
Okay.

125
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,280
I would like to reserve the superior suite.

126
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:53,760
Is breakfast included?

127
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,600
Yes, a buffet breakfast is served every morning.

128
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,560
I will need your name and your credit card details in order to complete the reservation.

129
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,420
Sure.

130
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:02,940
My credit card number is...

131
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,200
All right.

132
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:07,870
So now it's time for some phrases.

133
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,590
Let's start with Fluency Builder.

134
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:12,560
Fluency Builder.

135
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,580
The first phrase in Fluency Builder might seem a little bit strange.

136
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,980
It's I will be in town next week.

137
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:20,680
I'll be in town.

138
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:21,680
In what town?

139
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:22,440
That's right.

140
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:28,160
Well, if you say I will be in town, that basically says I will be in this town.

141
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:28,700
I will be there.

142
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:29,480
I will be here.

143
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,320
So, I'll be in the town you're in.

144
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:33,220
This is interesting.

145
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,960
So, when I'm talking to someone, maybe Marco is in Chicago and I'm in New York.

146
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,720
I call and say, hey, Marco, I'll be in town next week.

147
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:42,560
What are you doing?

148
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:43,140
Right.

149
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,040
I'm going to be in Chicago.

150
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,040
I want to have a drink.

151
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:47,040
That means I'm going to be where?

152
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,040
You're going to be in Chicago.

153
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,040
That's right.

154
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,040
I'll be in Chicago like Marco is.

155
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,640
I'm not going to talk about where I am now.

156
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:53,440
This usually means I'm going somewhere else.

157
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:54,240
That's right.

158
00:06:54,620 --> 00:07:01,680
So, actually, you can tell your friends that you're going to be in town or sometimes you have to tell someone you're going to be out of town.

159
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,100
I'll be out of town.

160
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,200
That means I won't be where I am now.

161
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,020
I won't be in New York.

162
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,240
I'll be somewhere else.

163
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,640
I'll be in Chicago.

164
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:08,840
That's right.

165
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:10,640
All right.

166
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:21,120
So, we had one where when we were talking specifically about the hotel and maybe what is included with our suite, we asked a very important question.

167
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,400
Is breakfast included?

168
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:23,910
Included in what?

169
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,230
In the price.

170
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:26,030
All right.

171
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,630
So, this is a very common question like you're saying, Marco, but it's not obvious.

172
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,130
So when you ask, is breakfast included?

173
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:35,880
That means do I have to pay extra for breakfast?

174
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:39,720
If breakfast is included, I don't have to pay.

175
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,890
If it's not included, that means I have to pay extra for breakfast.

176
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:43,920
That's right.

177
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:47,400
And in this case, breakfast is included, but not just any breakfast.

178
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,980
It's a buffet breakfast.

179
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,320
My favorite kind of breakfast.

180
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,660
So, this is pretty common with hotels.

181
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:58,240
They will serve a buffet breakfast from 7 a.m. to 9 a.m. or whatever.

182
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:02,260
A buffet means that there's a room with tables and food on the tables.

183
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:02,960
Right.

184
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,260
So, you don't order food.

185
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,980
You just take whatever you want.

186
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:06,580
That's right.

187
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,940
So, you can take whatever you want and usually as much as you want.

188
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:11,820
That's the best part.

189
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:12,700
Okay.

190
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:15,030
So, now we know that breakfast is included.

191
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:16,810
We know what a room is like.

192
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:25,110
So, we're going to make the reservation and the hotel employee says that he needs our credit card details to complete the reservation.

193
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:26,500
Credit card details.

194
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,460
Now, you might be wondering what details.

195
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:33,460
Credit card details means the specific information on your credit card.

196
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,280
All right.

197
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:38,120
So, it's pretty common when you're making a purchase on the phone or on the internet.

198
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:38,820
You have to enter.

199
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:40,820
You have to provide your credit card details.

200
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,080
Right.

201
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:50,220
That means your name, your credit card number, and the expiration date which is when the card will no longer be useful.

202
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:58,460
So, it's necessary because obviously you can say, yeah, I'm going to be there tomorrow and then you don't show up and the hotel loses money.

203
00:08:58,460 --> 00:09:00,980
So, they need to make sure that they have you somehow.

204
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:01,380
Yeah.

205
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:03,000
That's their way of protecting themselves.

206
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,480
They want to give you the room but they also don't want to lose money.

207
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,480
Okay.

208
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:11,180
So, let's listen to our dialogue one last time and we'll be back to talk a little bit more.

209
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,620
Madison Suites, how may I help you?

210
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,760
Yes, I am calling from Mexico.

211
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:26,280
I will be in town next week and would like to know if you have availability.

212
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:27,320
Okay, ma'am.

213
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,380
Can you tell me the date you expect to check in?

214
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:31,280
Yes, July 9th.

215
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,760
I will be there for seven nights.

216
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:37,540
We have a junior single suite or a superior double suite available for those dates.

217
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:38,620
What's the difference?

218
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:43,520
The junior suite is smaller and has one twin bed, while the superior suite has a double bed and minibar.

219
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:46,100
Okay, I would like to reserve the superior suite.

220
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:47,520
Is breakfast included?

221
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,080
Yes, a buffet breakfast is served every morning.

222
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:53,440
I will need your name and your credit card details in order to complete the reservation.

223
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:55,700
Sure, my credit card number is...

224
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:01,070
All right.

225
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:12,090
So talking about hotels, I think one of the most important things out of this, well, not important, but also something that you should know is that the minibar is always so expensive.

226
00:10:12,670 --> 00:10:13,590
It is expensive.

227
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:16,960
Be very careful when you're going into that minibar.

228
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,560
Sometimes it seems like a really good idea.

229
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,930
You're hungry and there are crackers or you want a beer.

230
00:10:20,930 --> 00:10:30,520
But you have to look at the menu because the menu will have the prices and maybe something that's really cheap in a store outside is really expensive at a hotel.

231
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:38,100
And I think sometimes, I don't know, sometimes it's even hard to find that little menu so you don't even know what the prices are.

232
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:42,400
But you're so thirsty, you just want to have something to drink now and it ends up costing you $10.

233
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:43,680
So, be careful.

234
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:48,900
Anytime you're in a hotel room, expect the prices to be pretty high for the things in the hotel.

235
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:55,280
Unless, of course, there's a sign or a piece of paper that says that something is free or complimentary.

236
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,380
Yeah, that's right.

237
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,000
Complimentary water is very common in hotels.

238
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,800
They'll give you two free bottles of water.

239
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:01,800
That's right.

240
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,560
So, complimentary means you don't have to pay for it.

241
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:06,020
But if there's no sign, then expect to pay a lot.

242
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:06,620
That's right.

243
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,480
Okay.

244
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:13,680
